PROJECT-SPECIFIC SAFETY AND LIABILITY NOTICE
DEYE ENERGY MANAGER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This notice explains the risks and responsibilities connected with the use of
Deye Energy Manager. It does not restrict the rights granted under the MIT
License above.

1. Software provided without warranty

Deye Energy Manager is provided free of charge as open-source software and
without any warranty of correct, safe, continuous or uninterrupted operation.

The Software may read data from and request changes to an inverter, battery
energy storage system, battery management system, meter and related Home
Assistant entities.

2. Full responsibility of the user

Every user installs, configures and uses the Software entirely at their own
risk and assumes full responsibility for:

- all configuration settings;
- all entity mappings;
- all commands sent to connected devices;
- inverter operating modes and export settings;
- battery charge and discharge currents;
- power limits and SOC limits;
- grid charging and Time Of Use schedules;
- safe default and emergency settings;
- automations, tariffs, prices, forecasts and AI suggestions;
- compatibility with the inverter, battery, BMS, meter, wiring, firmware and
  the electrical installation;
- backups, restoration procedures, supervision and testing of the installation.

The user is solely responsible for verifying all settings against current
manufacturer documentation, device ratings, warranty conditions, electrical
requirements, grid operator rules and the user's energy contract.

3. No liability of the author and contributors

The author, project owner and contributors shall not be held responsible for
any damage, failure, loss, cost, injury, claim or other consequence resulting
directly or indirectly from the installation, configuration, use, misuse,
malfunction, interruption or inability to use the Software.

This includes, without limitation:

- damage to an inverter, battery, BMS, meter, wiring, electrical installation
  or other property;
- overheating, fire, electric shock, personal injury or other safety incidents;
- battery degradation or reduced battery life;
- loss or corruption of data;
- loss of warranty;
- loss of energy, revenue or expected savings;
- increased electricity charges;
- unintended grid import or export;
- incorrect operation of schedules, automations, forecasts, optimization or AI
  functions;
- downtime and third-party claims.

By installing or using the Software, the user confirms that they understand
the associated risks, accept those risks and agree not to hold the author,
project owner or contributors responsible for the consequences of using the
Software.

4. Electrical and battery safety

Inverters and energy storage systems may involve dangerous voltages, high
currents, stored energy and remotely initiated operating changes. Incorrect
configuration, communication failure or equipment failure may cause serious
damage or injury.

The Software does not replace:

- hardware protection;
- circuit breakers, fuses, contactors or emergency disconnects;
- inverter or BMS protection functions;
- fire protection;
- inspections and maintenance;
- emergency procedures;
- work performed by a qualified electrician or installer.

The Software must not be treated as an emergency shutdown system, a life-safety
system or the sole means of preventing hazardous electrical, thermal or battery
conditions.

5. Automated operation

The Software may perform scheduled or automated control actions without
additional confirmation immediately before every action.

Before enabling automatic operation, the user must verify all schedules,
limits, protections, fallback settings and connected entities, and must test
the installation under safe conditions.

6. No professional, legal or financial advice

Schedules, forecasts, prices, statistics, AI output and optimization results
are informational only and may be incomplete, delayed or incorrect.

They do not constitute electrical, engineering, safety, legal or financial
advice and do not guarantee savings, revenue, availability or any particular
result.

7. Third-party systems and data

The Software may depend on Home Assistant, ESPHome, Solarman, inverter
firmware, external integrations, network connectivity, APIs, weather forecasts,
energy price data and AI providers.

The author and contributors do not control and do not guarantee the
availability, accuracy, security, compatibility or behaviour of those systems.

When the user enables an external API or AI provider, selected installation
data may be transmitted to that third-party service. The user is responsible
for reviewing the provider's terms and privacy policy, protecting API
credentials and deciding what data may be transmitted.

8. No affiliation or endorsement

Deye Energy Manager is an independent community project. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, sponsored by or officially supported by Deye, Home
Assistant, ESPHome, Solarman, any inverter or battery manufacturer, any energy
supplier or any grid operator.

All product names, company names and trademarks belong to their respective
owners.

